 /rsvp_boot?id=1631853\n\nDescription:\nThe Latine and Caribbean\, the Wome
 n and Gender Student Advising\, and the Men of Color Alliance (MoCA)\, bri
 ng a new Healing Across the Diaspora for the Men’s Mental Health Series 
 (MMHS) for the first MMHS celebration in Dartmouth's history.\nThis gather
 ing centers men's mental health and creates space to reflect on how we und
 erstand\, discuss\, and support men's well-being in the college community.
  Through conversation and reflection\, participants will explore new ways 
 of thinking about mental health\, connection\, vulnerability\, and support
  while considering how we can collectively reimagine what it means to care
  for men's mental health at Dartmouth.\nThe event is open to community mem
 bers who identify as men\, as well as those who wish to learn\, listen\, a
 nd engage in solidarity.\nRSVP through Dartmouth Groups. Lunch will be pro
 vided.\n\nSponsor / organizer: Office of Pluralism and Leadership\n\nSourc
