 s for students interested in exploring or pursuing careers for the common 
 good.\nThis panel\, co-sponsored and co-hosted with Dartmouth's Center for
  Career Design\, will provide direct insight from young alumni who have su
 ccessfully made the transition from student to young professional in their
  years immediately after Dartmouth. Brandon Green\, the CCD's "Good & Gree
 n" Career Coach\, will act as moderator\, guiding the conversation through
  the processes and emotions of job searching.\nBreakfast will be served. V
 egan\, vegetarian\, and gluten-free options will be available.\nIf you RSV
 P but become unable attend\, please email Sai Waters at sai.waters@dartmou
 th.edu by Tuesday\, October 20th so that we can offer your seat to a stude
 nt on the waitlist.\n-----------------------------------------------------
 -----------------------------------------------------------------------\nI
 n addition to this event\, there is an inaugural dinner and keynote from J
 im Bildner '75 on Thursday\, October 22nd. There will be a series of lunch
  panels around specific social impact themes on Friday\, October 23rd. See
  additional event postings for details.\nVisit DCSI's website for the late
 st updates and registration information along with details about alumni at
 tendees as they become available.\nFood Provided (Breakfast buffet with ve
 getarian\, vegan\, and gluten-free options available. )\n\nSponsor / organ
 izer: Dartmouth Center for Social Impact / Dartmouth Center for Career Des
