DESCRIPTION:Original event page(s):\nhttps://home.dartmouth.edu/events/eve
 nt?event=82542\n\nDescription:\nJoin us on October 23rd for our annual job
  search panel of this year's Breaking the Mold. Breaking the Mold is a 2-d
 ay conference sponsored by the Dartmouth Center for Social Impact (DCSI) t
 hat seeks to provide information and alumni networking opportunities for s
 tudents interested in exploring or pursuing careers for the common good.\n
 This panel\, co-sponsored and co-hosted with Dartmouth's Center for Career
  Design\, will provide direct insight from young alumni who have successfu
 lly made the transition from student to young professional in their years 
 immediately after Dartmouth. Brandon Green\, the CCD's "Good & Green" Care
 er Coach\, will act as moderator\, guiding the conversation through the pr
 ocesses and emotions of job searching.\nBreakfast will be served. Vegan\, 
 vegetarian\, and gluten-free options will be available.\n----\nPlease RSVP
  on Dartmouth Groups.\nIf you RSVP but become unable attend\, please email
  Sai Waters at sai.waters@dartmouth.edu by Tuesday\, October 20th so that 
 we can offer your seat to a student on the waitlist.\nIn addition to this 
 event\, there is an inaugural dinner and keynote from Jim Bildner '75 on T
 hursday\, October 22nd. There will be a series of lunch panels around spec
 ific social impact themes on Friday\, October 23rd. See additional event p
 ostings for details.\nVisit DCSI's website for the latest updates and regi
 stration information along with details about alumni attendees as they bec
 ome available.\n\nSponsor / organizer: Dartmouth Center for Social Impact\
 n\nAudience: Students-Graduate\, Students-Undergraduate\n\nSource: Dartmou
 th\n\nWhy this was included: Free Food category\; explicit food-service wo
 rding\; food keyword near service context\n\nFood availability is inferred
  from the source listing\; verify details before attending.
